  "observations": [
    "Stock richtap_file_mmap maps the 0x4000-byte node pool at state+0x610; the protection mask 0xfb includes VM_WRITE (0x2).",
    "Stock richtap_write is a stub returning count. Stock ioctl 0x5209 copies a separate RTP buffer at state+0x608; neither kernel path is the mapped FIFO producer.",
    "Stock Ghidra/assembly shows the worker and IRQ consume the mapped node state/length/payload. The hardened current candidate validates pool geometry and size bounds, but READ_ONCE/WRITE_ONCE are not an explicit userspace release/acquire protocol.",
    "Current candidate AArch64 assembly for the helper and worker contains no LDAR/STLR or DMB/DSB/ISB instructions in those function bodies. Their mapped FIFO metadata accesses compile to ordinary loads/stores; this says nothing about a userspace client that is absent from the evidence set.",
    "The corresponding stock helper, RTP worker and IRQ assembly/decompiles also contain no explicit LDAR/STLR or DMB/DSB/ISB operations at these consumer paths; the missing producer contract cannot be inferred from kernel-side synchronization.",
    "The kernel IRQ/worker mutex coordinates kernel consumers; a userspace writer cannot take that private kernel mutex. Concurrent payload modification and producer publication ordering therefore remain unverified."
